  "term": "neuritic plaque",
  "definition": "A neuritic plaque is a beta-amyloid plaque that can be seen with PET imaging using an amyloid-binding tracer. The amount of neuritic plaque present may be a sign of Alzheimer’s disease or other neurologic conditions.",
